I think it means "mi xunre". It's the same as
mi ckaji leka xunre
or such.

It only is the same as an abstract du'u if you were using it in an
abstract. So,
leka xagji keibe mi == ledu'u mi xagji
leseka xagji == le xagji
seka xagji == xagji
ka xagji keibe mi = du'u mi xagji

